"target_id":"80b1-6923-8fdc-41f2"},{"link_uuid":"0ab612c0-2583-43ae-a978-002a41034c4e","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"cb13-64ad-f0e0-47b6"},{"link_uuid":"db0e0a5d-afce-41fd-94ff-e9783d104b07","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"48d5-86e7-de52-4164"},{"link_uuid":"6b92dc34-4bcb-4f66-a3e3-5c528504e6a2","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"25b6-a320-d0ef-4e69"},{"link_uuid":"a2cd61c5-a92b-460c-ae6f-4da6c62b5aa5","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"3da4-47c0-e355-4e77"},{"link_uuid":"9eb23b5c-d0ab-4b1e-8660-e9486c9df9a8","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"6e56-240f-8519-4650"},{"link_uuid":"8cdc61a3-d433-4563-801a-989c0a05f341","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"6c75-e8ca-f36a-4f0c"},{"link_uuid":"a5ed2e67-bfab-4054-9e12-685c4624464d","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"448d-f11d-9439-4892"},{"link_uuid":"780ecdba-38ac-41a9-b8e5-874892c2b28a","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"e621-4cea-354c-46ff"},{"link_uuid":"2ef793e3-b89c-4c3b-aabd-7e1c4b834aeb","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"2cc3-d77d-f11a-4de0"},{"link_uuid":"cbe90fe6-b041-4725-a0a0-dd5bad69b82a","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"2b0e-6a55-c2de-43f4"},{"link_uuid":"66079856-9cbc-4ebf-bdf3-e96b7364f190","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"ed4c-eb8c-4691-4171"},{"link_uuid":"989da1a3-cc5c-47b0-a5cc-15119160d10d","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"4c52-dacc-9a0e-480a"},{"link_uuid":"e7005ed7-4864-4daf-a3bd-1243a9182f00","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"f566-67dd-9cbb-4d68"},{"link_uuid":"6af3cf72-96f5-49dd-8311-9c8737df0d06","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"601e-30a2-9b85-4c8a"},{"link_uuid":"6f50fd7c-4ca3-4d32-b4a4-aaf66bb78854","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"c635-5673-7a8b-45da"},{"link_uuid":"cdf707a2-2919-4a24-991b-e42f20648d34","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"f642-dfac-ae23-4f11"},{"link_uuid":"710e5eb1-4e7c-4c5a-a3a9-b7eb8413c996","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"722b-ec8d-8b47-4b28"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe tests/unit cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/unit/test_identity_ts2_09f9_heldout.py:1-13` — Preserve independent TS2 identity coverage. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_identity_ts2_09f9.py:1-8` — Preserve TS2 identity behavior. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_identity_ts3_117b_heldout.py:1-13` — Preserve independent TS3 identity coverage. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_identity_ts3_117b.py:1-9` — Preserve TS3 identity behavior. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_identity_txn_signing_heldout.py:1-11` — Preserve transactional identity-signing coverage. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_impact_code.py:1-27, 445-449` — Preserve code-impact extraction rules and edge cases. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_impact_model_versioning.py:1-9, 90-101, 120-133` — Preserve impact-model version compatibility and upgrade behavior. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_impact_plan.py:1-8, 229-232` — Preserve plan-impact extraction semantics. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_init_ensures_seam.py:1-15` — Preserve init-to-ensure delegation and monkeypatchability. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_interpret_failure_seam.py:1-20, 79-83, 117-121` — Preserve failure-interpretation delegation and compatibility seam. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_jira_dc_capability_map_workflow.py:1-14, 115-124, 128-138, 199-207, 220-227, 250-253, 307-316, 455-460` — Preserve Jira DC capability discovery, caching, fallback, and diagnostics. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_jira_onboard.py:1-14, 166-172` — Preserve Jira onboarding configuration and safe failure behavior. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_jira_snapshot_entry_schema.py:1-23` — Preserve snapshot-entry wire compatibility and required fields. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_json_or_narrowing.py:1-8` — Preserve JSON-or type narrowing. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_kind_wire_value_cutover_edge.py:1-7` — Preserve edge compatibility for kind wire values. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_last_pass_backoff_jitter_paediatric.py:1-12` — Preserve last-pass backoff jitter bounds. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_legacy_material_grandfather_96d1.py:1-15` — Preserve grandfathering of valid legacy material. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_legacy_signature_mirror_drop.py:37-40` — Preserve omission of legacy signatures from mirrors. Consumer: test maintainers.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by a row-by-row completion comment and the commands under Verification.\n- [ ] No executable behavior or test assertion changes; verified by the commands under Verification exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_identity_ts2_09f9_heldout.py tests/unit/test_identity_ts2_09f9.py tests/unit/test_identity_ts3_117b_heldout.py tests/unit/test_identity_ts3_117b.py tests/unit/test_identity_txn_signing_